<title>USA: Digital Microwave gets $17.8 mln deal.</title>
<headline>Digital Microwave gets $17.8 mln deal.</headline>
<dateline>SAN JOSE, Calif. 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Digital Microwave Corp said Monday it has received an order valued at $17.8 million.</p>
<p>The company said in a statement the contract is to supply digital microwave radios to Mutiara Telecom in Malaysia for the expansion of its nation-wide personal communications network.</p>
<p>Under the terms of this contract, Digital Microwave Corporation will provide 13 GHz and 18 GHz radios from its SPECTRUM II and QUANTUM families of radio products. Deliveries will begin immediately and are set to be completed during October 1997.</p>
</text>
